    "caveats": [
      "raw_payments.amount is stored in cents; divide by 100.0 to report dollar amounts.",
      "Payment records are transaction-level, not order-level: a single order can have multiple payments. Aggregate payment amounts to the order level before joining them to orders or customers when calculating order-level or customer-level revenue.",
      "Joining raw_orders directly to raw_payments duplicates order rows for orders with multiple payments. Do not use COUNT(*) after that join as an order count; use COUNT(DISTINCT raw_orders.id) or pre-aggregate payments.",
      "Not every customer necessarily has an order, and not every order necessarily has a payment; use LEFT JOINs when retaining unmatched customers or orders matters.",
      "Order status is the current order status and no status-history timestamp is available.",
      "Order dates span only 2018-01-01 through 2018-04-09, so period trends outside this range cannot be inferred.",
      "Payment amount may be zero, so payment transaction counts and paid-dollar totals describe different concepts."
    ],
    "example_questions": [
